^{x}-3xy,\\,y(-2)=3\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $Δx=1.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325169/selection/ma-v1/aa2ad8608cc2ceabe56e69cb977752c971139e3efe06b71dc1ea0453bc6bd8ed"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-333648/selection/d0e3ac7b3f806c73885c9b4b723d3bbf8a626eeeb82e0e35c40894cdd3f3df07" :answer/id #uuid "8d9d12f1-7ff6-50ff-a6d6-a6fe67cefbac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{1}{5}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)y+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333648/selection/f7f30abdeded0c565fc96cfc0717617f6a58e734443545b2336bcd3d773cf13e" :answer/id #uuid "7a46e7cd-ba54-5b20-8219-ce238f1cf37a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4-{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333648/selection/72a112b0418719d1447dc4a991feb5776132a5f400dbc2d5c62dd5320accd627" :answer/id #uuid "af85895f-3f7b-58b0-bb02-f83d43f74206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\\frac{1}{5}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333648/selection/b7838c48323a50fad34434d00cdd94ecaae1a0ef23986bc6166e4444c083b593" :answer/id #uuid "005b85cc-79ba-53e8-af18-11cabf0825b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333648/selection/735798cb3da5183629bb7d560a7e109e6bdddc415c11fd9d74ffe53ef9c92a25" :answer/id #uuid "5d1bf9d5-ab31-5340-9d22-ff956b5b3e2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333648/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f543f8ce-c6c5-5c9e-aa3d-d45fd66009a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-333648/selection/b7838c48323a50fad34434d00cdd94ecaae1a0ef23986bc6166e4444c083b593" :answer-field/choices ["q-333648/selection/d0e3ac7b3f806c73885c9b4b723d3bbf8a626eeeb82e0e35c40894cdd3f3df07" "q-333648/selection/f7f30abdeded0c565fc96cfc0717617f6a58e734443545b2336bcd3d773cf13e" "q-333648/selection/72a112b0418719d1447dc4a991feb5776132a5f400dbc2d5c62dd5320accd627" "q-333648/selection/b7838c48323a50fad34434d00cdd94ecaae1a0ef23986bc6166e4444c083b593" "q-333648/selection/735798cb3da5183629bb7d560a7e109e6bdddc415c11fd9d74ffe53ef9c92a25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333648" :question/id #uuid "b9c85170-a4b1-51b4-9704-03d5246a1950" :question/math-academy-id "q-333648" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+1)y+2x,\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{5}.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+2{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{5}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{5}{y}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{5}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}) & =y+\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ 5{y}_{\\text{new}}(\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) & =5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(4-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) & =5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{5y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}}{4-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-333648/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7095c46-33cf-5407-be83-70a49cf6eadd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333648"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339698/field-1/8baf9a862dcd52b8a24b5e3c26a10f8bf6cdd6d5aeefc479c7c6d64b5d111853" :answer/id #uuid "a590094d-1cdd-5c06-b85d-887b70c5bde8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339698/field-1/c2ec7d83bd2abf852a282dd8ec132009b07df4db2fc4a8535ae9d620bcbab6e5" :answer/id #uuid "dc892c02-c529-5b7d-96e9-a28df2c1696d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339698/field-1/13b5694d2972058414e339472820b3e7fb5d0a5ca42aa52a7e10b3ee5b426c91" :answer/id #uuid "254ba5f6-99ea-56f3-a6c5-f29d2bd44bef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339698/field-1/d4d4d9e92bd7bbb25122a5216e9b2f8b0951e78111b6aeadb336f5117e9f4aa2" :answer/id #uuid "9dd20ef0-88a6-5798-9838-9bc8abf99156" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.58" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339698/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "37a8f92c-c9d7-5da7-96c2-ebca0b24fccd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339698/field-1/d4d4d9e92bd7bbb25122a5216e9b2f8b0951e78111b6aeadb336f5117e9f4aa2" :answer-field/choices ["q-339698/field-1/8baf9a862dcd52b8a24b5e3c26a10f8bf6cdd6d5aeefc479c7c6d64b5d111853" "q-339698/field-1/c2ec7d83bd2abf852a282dd8ec132009b07df4db2fc4a8535ae9d620bcbab6e5" "q-339698/field-1/13b5694d2972058414e339472820b3e7fb5d0a5ca42aa52a7e10b3ee5b426c91" "q-339698/field-1/d4d4d9e92bd7bbb25122a5216e9b2f8b0951e78111b6aeadb336f5117e9f4aa2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339698" :question/id #uuid "117900e5-d11d-58f8-b65f-140bbdd217d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-339698" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=({x}^{2}+2)y+{e}^{x},\\,y(1)=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(2)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(2)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =((({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ (1-(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2)){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2)} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}+{e}^{2}}{1+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}+{e}^{2}}{5} \\\\  & ≈-1.58,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-1.58.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339698/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339698"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339695/field-1/37602717197d143418b60ff1098bab7e2dfeaad9ccb008e1ff70932092ab9b7c" :answer/id #uuid "3bdbfa2e-627e-5ca6-b759-2bb47921f7fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.99" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339695/field-1/2d8345de00526678cb5ec1387853baabb15a7081e06c1b73afb725357a5ef3f8" :answer/id #uuid "859fc32b-4b98-5422-9c06-481f0617aeb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.29" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339695/field-1/d0093d0b299790fb66e2264825c8fd36d46a8a0cf34c8c97bfba1ca28051d69a" :answer/id #uuid "0e039f09-3ee9-56cc-b63a-bad1e888a9df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339695/field-1/f5ca698e7cbf8c1f63a3d2e8be877e0d06359b03501146dff1a3eba9c17a5be7" :answer/id #uuid "76b69cff-d903-5eab-9dd2-fa3855878889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339695/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e475f53-b413-59a6-b2b1-cf341693d5bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339695/field-1/f5ca698e7cbf8c1f63a3d2e8be877e0d06359b03501146dff1a3eba9c17a5be7" :answer-field/choices ["q-339695/field-1/37602717197d143418b60ff1098bab7e2dfeaad9ccb008e1ff70932092ab9b7c" "q-339695/field-1/2d8345de00526678cb5ec1387853baabb15a7081e06c1b73afb725357a5ef3f8" "q-339695/field-1/d0093d0b299790fb66e2264825c8fd36d46a8a0cf34c8c97bfba1ca28051d69a" "q-339695/field-1/f5ca698e7cbf8c1f63a3d2e8be877e0d06359b03501146dff1a3eba9c17a5be7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339695" :question/id #uuid "3dd9c8e3-0a5f-5518-8268-fe808abca826" :question/math-academy-id "q-339695" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(2{e}^{x}+1),\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}\\cdot (2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{y}_{\\text{new}}(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-{y}_{\\text{new}}(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1) & =y \\\\ (1-(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1)){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{1-(2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+1)} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y}{2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =-\\frac{y}{2{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2e} \\\\  & ≈-0.18,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈-0.18.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339695/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339691/field-1/136ef958a666e466a998d299ea8fffbb56191965b6e769fa603ff08408ec117b" :answer/id #uuid "d50a28f9-cb8f-56b3-a1f9-1056ca545f34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339691/field-1/3abcae015e20f845a45fe844291a7696b0e5089e92034112489f446cfd05e68c" :answer/id #uuid "a6dfc6d1-904a-5609-b822-4e79c4c46b38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339691/field-1/6b9ae919f8dc19b90b31dd7dbbd73f5656fef6a8e72ae9ea4a0797925a9e2bc9" :answer/id #uuid "a9482fcf-7fdd-535d-be01-fa12386d052b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.01" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339691/field-1/82ee0ad984b180e3da43b631af39d78de4dccdd3c66641b901f329ec15284009" :answer/id #uuid "2d3833d5-3283-5935-a734-f45b4ae49193" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.71" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339691/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6a75e46-943f-5a9b-9e6d-4d9b80905b8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339691/field-1/136ef958a666e466a998d299ea8fffbb56191965b6e769fa603ff08408ec117b" :answer-field/choices ["q-339691/field-1/136ef958a666e466a998d299ea8fffbb56191965b6e769fa603ff08408ec117b" "q-339691/field-1/3abcae015e20f845a45fe844291a7696b0e5089e92034112489f446cfd05e68c" "q-339691/field-1/6b9ae919f8dc19b90b31dd7dbbd73f5656fef6a8e72ae9ea4a0797925a9e2bc9" "q-339691/field-1/82ee0ad984b180e3da43b631af39d78de4dccdd3c66641b901f329ec15284009"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339691" :question/id #uuid "f75dcc74-76ed-50af-9566-63f6f6a83994" :question/math-academy-id "q-339691" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-4x,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(2)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(2)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-0=2.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-4{x}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-8{x}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-8{x}_{\\text{new}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-8{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ (1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-8{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y-8{x}_{\\text{new}}}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+2=2.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y-8{x}_{\\text{new}}}{1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-8\\cdot 2}{1-2\\cdot {2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{7} \\\\  & ≈2.14,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈2.14.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339691/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339696/field-1/8d928f53285064af63f9aa4dd47142c6e2eadde48b47c13c3ee14ff6c7dc3309" :answer/id #uuid "6f224b64-f2da-5af3-8c01-5930b5b9ca1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339696/field-1/5042a0651ef29f53af4cf52ea2d8dda9d3c6af1ec8fab9808c8a91b5fd3a237f" :answer/id #uuid "0ca38e60-6b45-5e65-8da7-9dcae8d7417b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.39" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339696/field-1/68d660245faa6640cb843d3998464f4b779fab9f99ac71d5091750d84d3b0b6d" :answer/id #uuid "15be0de3-a3a7-541e-9f80-88d1acad2188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339696/field-1/7074de4862785308050214a62915e33bc422290f9ace9ebfd7905084dfdcacab" :answer/id #uuid "a3100e1e-1b4d-5ee4-bfff-3219b3e862cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339696/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2032e6b7-15c6-5a51-9c0a-d0f3e7e39672" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339696/field-1/68d660245faa6640cb843d3998464f4b779fab9f99ac71d5091750d84d3b0b6d" :answer-field/choices ["q-339696/field-1/8d928f53285064af63f9aa4dd47142c6e2eadde48b47c13c3ee14ff6c7dc3309" "q-339696/field-1/5042a0651ef29f53af4cf52ea2d8dda9d3c6af1ec8fab9808c8a91b5fd3a237f" "q-339696/field-1/68d660245faa6640cb843d3998464f4b779fab9f99ac71d5091750d84d3b0b6d" "q-339696/field-1/7074de4862785308050214a62915e33bc422290f9ace9ebfd7905084dfdcacab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339696" :question/id #uuid "72f212ba-86d7-561e-adb0-0049c49bcba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339696" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y(4{e}^{x}-2),\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}\\cdot (4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{y}_{\\text{new}}(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-{y}_{\\text{new}}(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2) & =y \\\\ (1-(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2)){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{1-(4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-2)} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{3-4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y}{3-4{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3-4{e}^{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3-4e} \\\\  & ≈-0.25,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈-0.25.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339696/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "246a84b2-e9fa-58e5-858c-66c09e1c3bc0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339696"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220659 :answer-field/correct 17592186220661 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-339635"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y({x}^{2}+1),\\,y(-1)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=-\\frac{1}{2}-(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}\\cdot (({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1) & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y}{1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y}{1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{1-{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & ≈2.67,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈2.67.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-1/e3be7b48e2c67f5b98b4cc20c09980c764eeb6fd7e7c5efeaf45429183e07bf9" :answer/id #uuid "ef628596-caeb-53ec-a5fa-875de436d987" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-1/3ae3abb3bec31a8544ca69be63953d13b4c44a3f80b6d577aeae2c9c12f41c52" :answer/id #uuid "c750f542-1d15-5a98-851e-3157a8a07c5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-1/607563974288a4b93a19d00d5c7f7e6283b5a0c28a65056c74a1bae643bdc9a2" :answer/id #uuid "751ed622-c5b5-5ef5-96d8-50ec69c70cd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8337ebdb-7432-534c-aba8-1a8f1e5c3a48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339720/field-1/607563974288a4b93a19d00d5c7f7e6283b5a0c28a65056c74a1bae643bdc9a2" :answer-field/choices ["q-339720/field-1/e3be7b48e2c67f5b98b4cc20c09980c764eeb6fd7e7c5efeaf45429183e07bf9" "q-339720/field-1/3ae3abb3bec31a8544ca69be63953d13b4c44a3f80b6d577aeae2c9c12f41c52" "q-339720/field-1/607563974288a4b93a19d00d5c7f7e6283b5a0c28a65056c74a1bae643bdc9a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-2/02190edabe4249cde304eaa81e13a6583e340c89664d88b02f4e88cb73323e39" :answer/id #uuid "cc7569df-46eb-56bd-be3d-e8ca00b0523a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-2/ce0f44764da0863e2db9a283de96fcdfeaaf9e2d330cbf67afd9e53d8813ec2e" :answer/id #uuid "fae59ae0-54e9-594f-8cd8-c7c6443fcc05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-2/b9cac57b15c8a2406cd697b222b8a41c064b8a7b7b8cfdd96e60c544359c1ab1" :answer/id #uuid "2896d3f8-fae6-5772-891c-23c8db39be68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6407a46a-12bc-51b5-b3cd-9d0308928f3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339720/field-2/02190edabe4249cde304eaa81e13a6583e340c89664d88b02f4e88cb73323e39" :answer-field/choices ["q-339720/field-2/02190edabe4249cde304eaa81e13a6583e340c89664d88b02f4e88cb73323e39" "q-339720/field-2/ce0f44764da0863e2db9a283de96fcdfeaaf9e2d330cbf67afd9e53d8813ec2e" "q-339720/field-2/b9cac57b15c8a2406cd697b222b8a41c064b8a7b7b8cfdd96e60c544359c1ab1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339720" :question/id #uuid "d7d1b30e-1b06-58e8-b5bd-fe8664e41f56" :question/math-academy-id "q-339720" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1-{x}^{2}+3{x}^{2}y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})+\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})+\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ (1-\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) \\\\ 2(1-\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+(1-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2-3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2-3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1}{2-3{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=2.2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2-3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2.2-{1}^{2}+1}{2-3\\cdot {1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-4.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈2.20,\\,y(1)≈-4.40.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339720/field-1" "q-339720/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-1/6c3fe5936b48b6895a0cca907277410fe16fa6a16cf280ebb305d391a97cd1f3" :answer/id #uuid "f7e75089-0d73-5b3e-bf31-5122bfadcecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-1/867645cc65f2523d2da0f0bf9f79dcff4e4758e45f7d0d53126cc6ed4f8a9875" :answer/id #uuid "a8bbc796-9cb2-5c5f-930a-feaf2befcff4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-1/e3be7b48e2c67f5b98b4cc20c09980c764eeb6fd7e7c5efeaf45429183e07bf9" :answer/id #uuid "e394f15f-188f-5b12-916a-240a7a94dff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9ff7a3-69ab-5583-a2f7-cce9862de625" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339713/field-1/867645cc65f2523d2da0f0bf9f79dcff4e4758e45f7d0d53126cc6ed4f8a9875" :answer-field/choices ["q-339713/field-1/6c3fe5936b48b6895a0cca907277410fe16fa6a16cf280ebb305d391a97cd1f3" "q-339713/field-1/867645cc65f2523d2da0f0bf9f79dcff4e4758e45f7d0d53126cc6ed4f8a9875" "q-339713/field-1/e3be7b48e2c67f5b98b4cc20c09980c764eeb6fd7e7c5efeaf45429183e07bf9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-2/3ae3abb3bec31a8544ca69be63953d13b4c44a3f80b6d577aeae2c9c12f41c52" :answer/id #uuid "def0ac28-809a-55c1-b573-08633d6e1560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-2/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7" :answer/id #uuid "4c97e05d-0d0b-5310-8c8d-716e50359af1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-2/c1705b6d118283209be8c1f6b060044945091b3980745a9fd18258cff12f328d" :answer/id #uuid "d10bedc6-5e19-5d83-8d29-b481f61c22f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "489bd6e7-d489-5177-9a72-d4be5ff94ba3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339713/field-2/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-339713/field-2/3ae3abb3bec31a8544ca69be63953d13b4c44a3f80b6d577aeae2c9c12f41c52" "q-339713/field-2/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7" "q-339713/field-2/c1705b6d118283209be8c1f6b060044945091b3980745a9fd18258cff12f328d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339713" :question/id #uuid "014d3463-d63f-5c65-a554-dfe15b02a633" :question/math-academy-id "q-339713" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-x-3y,\\,y(-1)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(0)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(-1)$ and asked to find $y(0).$ The distance from $x=-1$ to $x=0$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{0-(-1)}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{1}{2})}{5} \\\\  & =0.50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=0.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2\\cdot y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0.5-0}{5} \\\\  & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(-\\frac{1}{2})≈0.50,\\,y(0)≈0.20.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339713/field-1" "q-339713/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339713"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-1/e3be7b48e2c67f5b98b4cc20c09980c764eeb6fd7e7c5efeaf45429183e07bf9" :answer/id #uuid "23ab9d4f-3ad5-5b22-8761-1f5fcb40b471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-1/3ae3abb3bec31a8544ca69be63953d13b4c44a3f80b6d577aeae2c9c12f41c52" :answer/id #uuid "e102d97e-ad41-5e05-9f03-67896a5930ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-1/9249ec38b82e800720a79ba1072f7d45fcdfddce5a4914d085b8568b9b083f3a" :answer/id #uuid "c1b91a3d-e960-5ed1-97e9-5ebe2acb0307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b93524ca-c3a0-5702-a487-5b79800baab9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339719/field-1/9249ec38b82e800720a79ba1072f7d45fcdfddce5a4914d085b8568b9b083f3a" :answer-field/choices ["q-339719/field-1/e3be7b48e2c67f5b98b4cc20c09980c764eeb6fd7e7c5efeaf45429183e07bf9" "q-339719/field-1/3ae3abb3bec31a8544ca69be63953d13b4c44a3f80b6d577aeae2c9c12f41c52" "q-339719/field-1/9249ec38b82e800720a79ba1072f7d45fcdfddce5a4914d085b8568b9b083f3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-2/1429fa6c8ea2460ff4e95956555326814a94d00a66bfbde0268929e24d0f9512" :answer/id #uuid "30bc1266-281b-560a-901c-23c4ff4406be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-2/80e2916eb5934ea1ef2f974607266e92ecc465a102b1e6e527ae7ff4e271e127" :answer/id #uuid "a63f8e96-03af-5828-880b-623ddbc76c7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-2/e39cff96704a0d69356d02d3c63a221633678289ca4d5ae7fa2bedd21ff776d2" :answer/id #uuid "8c239742-99c5-5549-8bc7-eee961f5b6e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a69ffcba-ac19-5039-bc40-9e55ea4b81cf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339719/field-2/1429fa6c8ea2460ff4e95956555326814a94d00a66bfbde0268929e24d0f9512" :answer-field/choices ["q-339719/field-2/1429fa6c8ea2460ff4e95956555326814a94d00a66bfbde0268929e24d0f9512" "q-339719/field-2/80e2916eb5934ea1ef2f974607266e92ecc465a102b1e6e527ae7ff4e271e127" "q-339719/field-2/e39cff96704a0d69356d02d3c63a221633678289ca4d5ae7fa2bedd21ff776d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339719" :question/id #uuid "d535d60e-4068-5729-99a4-38ae3581a9c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-339719" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2}y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$$\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1-2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)-({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ (1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)}{1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1}{2+2{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=1.3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1.3+{1}^{2}+1}{2+2({1}^{2})} \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈1.30,\\,y(1)≈1.15.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339719/field-1" "q-339719/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220668 :answer-field/correct 17592186220671 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220664 :answer-field/correct 17592186220666 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-339642"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x-3y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(1)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+\\frac{1}{2})}{5} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=0.6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(0.6+1)}{5} \\\\  & =0.64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈0.60,\\,y(1)≈0.64.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-1/0bd67a2469fd62b372d3c18efb9f9145b88d10674f12435398ce87438b86e961" :answer/id #uuid "832ec1df-cf30-5e90-b68c-7ad3e8eb253d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-1/98ac0e3657c9982594ecf211d93b64061619bc44dc7ef9220733e0ee5224fcd3" :answer/id #uuid "81ad7101-0c1b-52af-a337-bcfcd6bef27e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.00" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-1/3c17e895c81d7cedfc69c2dc0ccf2e57c21909185f0a1fa438261e0f08654f43" :answer/id #uuid "74c12d69-14f3-54a3-98c2-ce099fc1b29a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.67" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7da530-e5be-5af4-8b91-6b697cd3bda7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339717/field-1/0bd67a2469fd62b372d3c18efb9f9145b88d10674f12435398ce87438b86e961" :answer-field/choices ["q-339717/field-1/0bd67a2469fd62b372d3c18efb9f9145b88d10674f12435398ce87438b86e961" "q-339717/field-1/98ac0e3657c9982594ecf211d93b64061619bc44dc7ef9220733e0ee5224fcd3" "q-339717/field-1/3c17e895c81d7cedfc69c2dc0ccf2e57c21909185f0a1fa438261e0f08654f43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-2/3008834d21908e89ca10fdb2d66a7a8f10650f7668405cab51ba305ad1aedc08" :answer/id #uuid "34a8de28-e521-5e32-adb7-fe650e9969c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.67" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-2/b8a8ec49b7ad259fcb2fe5620c72699ce9777d9568dd4a52a0543e69b979148b" :answer/id #uuid "fc7858e2-6996-5fa0-a0a3-bbcc71adede3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-2/ed6fd16bca6c793488ec1e91f183fc8be079b4298edea75b8906369e3c998626" :answer/id #uuid "6d2538f6-dcd1-5c6a-8255-b7b3bf0ce31d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11.00" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f48b26b1-1c64-562b-ae38-3c05070930c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339717/field-2/ed6fd16bca6c793488ec1e91f183fc8be079b4298edea75b8906369e3c998626" :answer-field/choices ["q-339717/field-2/3008834d21908e89ca10fdb2d66a7a8f10650f7668405cab51ba305ad1aedc08" "q-339717/field-2/b8a8ec49b7ad259fcb2fe5620c72699ce9777d9568dd4a52a0543e69b979148b" "q-339717/field-2/ed6fd16bca6c793488ec1e91f183fc8be079b4298edea75b8906369e3c998626"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339717" :question/id #uuid "8baedbb2-ab4c-580d-acaf-08d946efa9a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339717" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3x+y,\\,y(-1)=2\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0)$  rounded to $2$ decimal places.$\\,y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,y(0)≈$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(-1)$ and asked to find $y(0).$ The distance from $x=-1$ to $x=0$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{0-(-1)}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-3{x}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y-\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y-3{x}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y-3{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=5.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y-3{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5.5-3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(-\\frac{1}{2})≈5.50,\\,y(0)≈11.00.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339717/field-1" "q-339717/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "56e30ebf-9265-5ba8-888d-6956206b542e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21312"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = 2x^2+3xy, \\qquad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nThe **implicit** Euler method is applied with step size $\\Delta x = 1.$ \nFind the general formula for the new $y$ value, $y_\\text{new},$ in terms of the new value $x_\\text{new}$ and the current value $y.$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}+3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}}(1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}) & =y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+2{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21318"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = x^2y + e^x, \\qquad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with one step to approximate $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=\\dfrac12,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac12 - 0 = \\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In our case,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ (1-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is $x_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 0 + \\dfrac12 = \\dfrac12.$ Hence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{1/2}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(\\sqrt{e}-2)}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right) = \\dfrac{4}{7} \\left(\\sqrt{e} - 2\\right).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21661"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = 4x^2 - y, \\qquad y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUse the **implicit** Euler method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right)$ and $y(1).$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y_0 = y(x_0),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = y'_\\text{new} \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new},y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{1-0}2 = \\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(4({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y$ and solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y\\left(\\dfrac12\\right)$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx = 0,\\qquad y = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = 0 + \\dfrac12 = \\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(0+2{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac12, \\qquad y = \\dfrac13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\nx_\\text{new} = x + \\Delta x = \\dfrac12 + \\dfrac12 = 1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(\\frac{1}{3}+2\\cdot {1}^{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny\\left(\\dfrac12\\right)\\approx\\dfrac{1}{3}, \\qquad\ny(1)\\approx\\dfrac{14}{9}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
